{#
  melt's `page` layout is an ALIAS for the `article` shape.

  Every melt content page declares `bloob-shape: article` (2026-07-27), so this
  file is only reached by the preprocessor's step-5 default — an ordinary page
  whose declared shape does not exist yet, e.g. `bloob-shape: guide` before a
  `guide` shape is built. See shapes.md → "Unknown shape names".

  It cannot simply be deleted: the fallback resolves to the literal path
  `layouts/page.njk`, so Eleventy needs the file to exist. Making it an alias
  means an un-built shape degrades to melt's real page treatment rather than to
  a second, drifting copy of it.

  Content flows through once: this template emits the page body, and that output
  becomes `content` for article.njk, which supplies the header, dates, share bar
  and comments.
#}
